{
  "description": "Member-key and metadata-size vectors. Two independent contracts share this file because both pin the leaderboard/member write surface. `regex`/`valid`/`invalid` mirror counter-keys.json for member keys (openapi.yaml MemberKey: pattern ^[A-Za-z0-9._:@|-]+$, maxLength 256). `metadata` pins the Metadata cap (openapi.yaml Metadata: 1024 UTF-8 BYTES, counted as bytes not characters): every string in metadata.valid must pass client-side length validation, every string in metadata.invalid must be rejected locally before any request. Matching is exact and case-sensitive; no trimming.",
  "regex": "^[A-Za-z0-9._:@|-]{1,256}$",
  "maxLength": 256,
  "valid": [
    "playerX",
    "alice|bob",
    "a",
    "user@host",
    "a.b_c:d@e|f-g",
    "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa"
  ],
  "invalid": [
    "",
    "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa",
    "has space",
    "a/b",
    "a#b",
    "héro",
    "line\nbreak"
  ],
  "metadata": {
    "maxBytes": 1024,
    "encoding": "utf-8",
    "note": "The cap is 1024 UTF-8 bytes, NOT 1024 characters. The 341x'€'+'a' valid case is 1024 bytes (341*3+1) but only 342 characters; the 342x'€' invalid case is 1026 bytes but only 342 characters — an SDK that counts characters instead of bytes would wrongly accept it.",
